# DI Service Lifetimes

.NET provides three common service lifetimes:

| Lifetime      | Meaning                                                      |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Transient** | A new instance is created each time the service is requested |
| **Scoped**    | One instance is created per scope/request                    |
| **Singleton** | One instance is shared for the entire application lifetime   |

---

## 1. Transient

```csharp
builder.Services.AddTransient<IEmailService, EmailService>();
```

A new instance is created every time the service is requested.

### 🧠 Use when:

> **Need a fresh instance each time? → Transient**

Good for lightweight, stateless services.

---

## 2. Scoped

```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IOrderService, OrderService>();
```

One instance is created for each scope.

In a typical ASP.NET Core web application:

```text
HTTP Request
     │
     ├── OrderService → Instance A
     ├── OrderService → Instance A
     └── OrderService → Instance A

Next HTTP Request
     │
```
